==Trivia==
*Every name in this sub-chapter is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|alien]]-related reference:
**Area 22 is a reference to [[wikipedia:Area 51|Area 51]], which is commonly associated with aliens due to rumors.
**[[Roswell Incident]] is named after the [[wikipedia:Roswell UFO incident|Roswell UFO Incident]], an incident in mid-1947 in which a "flying disc" crashed at a ranch near Roswell, New Mexico.
**[[Cat Abduction]] refers to [[wikipedia:Alien abduction|alien abduction]], perhaps specifically [[Star Peng]]'s Warp ability. Its Japanese name, Cat Mutilation (キャットミューティレーション), is instead a reference to [[wikipedia:Cattle mutilation|cattle mutilation]].
**[[Adamski Type]] is named after [[wikipedia:George Adamski|George Adamski]], a Polish author who purported to have met extraterrestrials.
**[[Chupacabra Love]] is named after the [[wikipedia:Chupacabra|Chupacabra]], an alien-like legendary creature in the folklore of parts of the Americas, with its first purported sightings reported in Puerto Rico.
**[[Tunguska Event]] shares its name with the [[wikipedia:Tunguska event|Tunguska event]], an enormous explosion that occurred near the Stony Tunguska River in Yeniseysk Governorate, Russia, on the morning of 30 June 1908. Though believed to have been caused by the airburst of a small comet or meteorite, science fiction often attributes the event to aliens, such as in the short story "[[wikipedia:The Second Missile|The Second Missile]]".
**[[Offworld Weary]]'s Japanese name, Anata Tsukareteru no yo (あなた疲れてるのよ, "It is That You Are Tired"), is a reference to "[https://dic.pixiv.net/a/モルダー、あなた疲れてるのよ Mulder, anata tsukareteru no yo]" (モルダー、あなた疲れてるのよ, "Mulder, it is that you are tired"), a supposed "famous quote" from [[wikipedia:TV Asahi|TV Asahi]]'s Japanese dub of ''[[wikipedia:The X-Files|The X-Files]]'' wherein [[wikipedia:Dana Scully|Dana Scully]] dismisses her partner [[wikipedia:Fox Mulder|Fox Mulder]]'s belief in paranormal phenomena by insisting that he has simply gone crazy from tiredness. The actual origin of the quote is unknown, as while similar lines are said in episodes 7 and 21 of season 1, this exact phrase is not in any official dub, giving it a similar status to ''[[wikipedia:Star Trek|Star Trek]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s "[[wikipedia:Beam me up, Scotty|Beam me, up Scotty]]".

